{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-37270" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the eigenvectors of the $2\\times 2$ matrix $B$ given that \n\n$$\nB[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066049/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a6efe70f913ac229aee69f8912e1a9696608b9cb84deb88419fa9c2cdf97072"} {"question" "q-37270" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that the matrix $[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}]$ appears on both sides of the equation. Since this matrix is invertible (its determinant is not zero), right-multiplying the equation by the inverse gives the following expression for $B:$\n\n$$\nB={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{P}{{[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{D}{{{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}}_{⏟}}_{{P}^{-1}}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $B$ is diagonalizable. The eigenvalues of $B$ are ${\\lambda }_{1}=2$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=3$ and the corresponding eigenvectors are the columns of the matrix $P:$\n\n$\\,$ ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,{v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066049/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a6efe70f913ac229aee69f8912e1a9696608b9cb84deb88419fa9c2cdf97072"} {"question" "q-37270" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066049/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ae6990cd4e9a522228d2d882f29c3f128d059f74d476cbccc3616545ef941417"} {"question" "q-37270" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066049/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a6efe70f913ac229aee69f8912e1a9696608b9cb84deb88419fa9c2cdf97072"} {"question" "q-37270" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$ and $[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]$"] ["text" "$[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ and $[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$"] ["text" "$[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$ and $[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$"] ["text" "$[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$ and $[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$"] ["text" "$[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$ and $[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066049/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a6efe70f913ac229aee69f8912e1a9696608b9cb84deb88419fa9c2cdf97072"} {"question" "q-37270" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$ and $[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066049/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a6efe70f913ac229aee69f8912e1a9696608b9cb84deb88419fa9c2cdf97072"} {"question" "q-37625" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find ${A}^{69}$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]{[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -6\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066049/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a6efe70f913ac229aee69f8912e1a9696608b9cb84deb88419fa9c2cdf97072"} {"question" "q-37625" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We have been given the following diagonalization of $A.$\n\n$$\nA={{[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -6\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{P}{{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{D}{{{[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -6\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}}_{⏟}}_{{P}^{-1}}\n$$\n\nSo, since $A=PD{P}^{-1}$, we can compute ${A}^{k}$ by using the formula \n\n$$\n{A}^{k}=P{D}^{k}{P}^{-1}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the inverse of the matrix $P.$ We get\n\n$$\n{[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -6\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{12}[\\begin{aligned}-6 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nCarrying out the necessary multiplication, we obtain the following:\n\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{69} & =P{D}^{69}{P}^{-1} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -6\\end{aligned}]{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]}^{69}{[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -6\\end{aligned}]}^{-1} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{1}^{69} & 0 \\\\ 0 & (-1)^{69}\\end{aligned}](\\frac{1}{12}[\\begin{aligned}-6 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-6 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-6 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{2}{3} \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066049/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a6efe70f913ac229aee69f8912e1a9696608b9cb84deb88419fa9c2cdf97072"} {"question" "q-37625" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066049/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ae6990cd4e9a522228d2d882f29c3f128d059f74d476cbccc3616545ef941417"} {"question" "q-37625" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066049/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a6efe70f913ac229aee69f8912e1a9696608b9cb84deb88419fa9c2cdf97072"} {"question" "q-37625" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & \\frac{3}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{2}{3} \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3} & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3} & 0 \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066049/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a6efe70f913ac229aee69f8912e1a9696608b9cb84deb88419fa9c2cdf97072"} {"question" "q-37625" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{2}{3} \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066049/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a6efe70f913ac229aee69f8912e1a9696608b9cb84deb88419fa9c2cdf97072"} {"question" "q-86693" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the eigenvectors of the $2\\times 2$ matrix $B$ given that \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}8 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{aligned}]B=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 7\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}8 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066049/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a6efe70f913ac229aee69f8912e1a9696608b9cb84deb88419fa9c2cdf97072"} {"question" "q-86693" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that the matrix $[\\begin{aligned}8 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{aligned}]$ appears on both sides of the equation. Since this matrix is invertible (its determinant is not zero), left-multiplying the equation by the inverse gives the following expression for $B:$ \n\n$$\nB={{{[\\begin{aligned}8 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}}_{⏟}}_{P}{{[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 7\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{D}{{[\\begin{aligned}8 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{P}^{-1}}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $B$ is diagonalizable. The eigenvalues of $B$ are ${\\lambda }_{1}=-2$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=7$ and the corresponding eigenvectors are the columns of the matrix $P.$ Computing $P,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P={[\\begin{aligned}8 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{1}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ -5 & 8\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ -5 & 8\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn conclusion, the corresponding eigenvectors are: \n\n$\\,$ ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,{v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066049/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a6efe70f913ac229aee69f8912e1a9696608b9cb84deb88419fa9c2cdf97072"} {"question" "q-86693" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066049/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ae6990cd4e9a522228d2d882f29c3f128d059f74d476cbccc3616545ef941417"} {"question" "q-86693" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066049/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a6efe70f913ac229aee69f8912e1a9696608b9cb84deb88419fa9c2cdf97072"} {"question" "q-86693" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]$ and $[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]$"] ["text" "$[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]$ and $[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]$"] ["text" "$[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]$ and $[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]$"] ["text" "$[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]$ and $[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$"] ["text" "$[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]$ and $[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066049/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a6efe70f913ac229aee69f8912e1a9696608b9cb84deb88419fa9c2cdf97072"} {"question" "q-86693" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]$ and $[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]$"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066049/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a6efe70f913ac229aee69f8912e1a9696608b9cb84deb88419fa9c2cdf97072"} {"question" "q-140131" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find ${B}^{120},$ where\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[60]{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt[40]{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ -3 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066049/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a6efe70f913ac229aee69f8912e1a9696608b9cb84deb88419fa9c2cdf97072"} {"question" "q-140131" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, notice that\n\n$$\n{[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ -3 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we have been given the following diagonalization of $B:$\n\n$$\nB={{[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{P}{{[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[60]{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt[40]{2}\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{D}{{{[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}}_{⏟}}_{{P}^{-1}}\n$$\n\nSince $B=PD{P}^{-1}$, we can compute ${B}^{k}$ by using the formula \n\n$$\n{B}^{k}=P{D}^{k}{P}^{-1}.\n$$\n\nCarrying out the necessary multiplication, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{B}^{120} & =P{D}^{120}{P}^{-1} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}]{[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[60]{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt[40]{2}\\end{aligned}]}^{120}[\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ -3 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}(\\sqrt[60]{2})^{120} & 0 \\\\ 0 & (\\sqrt[40]{2})^{120}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ -3 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{2}^{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & {2}^{3}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ -3 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 8\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ -3 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-8 & -24 \\\\ 12 & 32\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ -3 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}40 & 24 \\\\ -48 & -28\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066049/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a6efe70f913ac229aee69f8912e1a9696608b9cb84deb88419fa9c2cdf97072"} {"question" "q-140131" "field" nil "attribute" "question/dif